# Shell scripts and CI definitions MUST reach the runner with LF endings.
#
# This does not depend on a contributor's core.autocrlf: a checkout on Windows with
# autocrlf=false commits CRLF verbatim, and a CRLF resolve.sh then fails on the Ubuntu
# runner with `$'\r': command not found` — an error that names neither the file nor the
# real cause. Pinning `eol=lf` makes the working copy LF everywhere too.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# The suite and its tooling run on Linux CI; keep them byte-identical there.
*.ts text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
